  "description": "Global Offshore Wind Technical Potential is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Extractive industries\", published or maintained by World Bank Group. This dataset presents the technical potential for offshore wind development at the country level, split into potential for fixed and floating foundations. The files are grouped per WB regions and delivered in.SHP,.KMZ (CRS:4326) and. EXCEL format. Coverage: 187 countries in East Asia and the Pacific, Europe and Central Asia, the Middle East and North Africa, South Asia. It has 17 files in HTML, ZIP, XLS. The portal files it under Extractive industries. The portal gives 2021 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. Suitability for infrastructure simulation has not been checked. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
